# The build context is the repository root, because the image needs backend/ and qdrant/ which
# live in different directories. Without this file that context is 68 GB: Docker Desktop's own
# data root was relocated to D:\AIRA\docker-data (62 GB), and the virtualenv, the model weights
# and the uv cache account for most of the rest. The first build attempt sat on "load build
# context" until it was killed.
#
# What the image actually needs is about 10 MB: the application, the requirements file, the
# incident database and the vector store.

# Docker's own storage, relocated here. Never send this anywhere.
docker-data/

# Local model weights - the image does not run Ollama.
ollama-models/

# Rebuilt inside the image from requirements.txt.
backend/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Caches: uv wheels and the fastembed model, both re-fetched during the build.
.cache/

# The monitored application. AIRA watches it; it is not part of AIRA.
opentelemetry-demo/

# Development output with no place in a deployed image.
logs/
.git/
node_modules/
*.log

# Scripts and docs are not served by the backend.
scripts/
docs/
deck/

# Local environment files must never reach an image that gets pushed anywhere.
.env
*.env
